 "_README": [
  "Depth below the body surface for every shipped structure of the Visible Human FEMALE (mm; shallowest point and median over the structure's surface), as computed by scripts/export_viewer_bundle.py (add_skin_depth) for the female bundle. Her body surface is the CT body silhouette (HU > -300) of BOTH CT blocks united on one grid (scripts/cryo/vhf_whole_body_skin.py) plus, above RAS z -950, the photograph silhouette of the registered cryosections for the ARMS the CT clips (scripts/cryo/vhf_skin_union.py); the trunk and legs stay CT-exact, the arm surface is +-10 mm. Derived data, regenerated 2026-09-12 after the lower-limb block, deltoid, rotator cuff, erector columns, upper-arm muscles and pectoralis minor were added; the legs->torso registration is +-4 mm in height, which bounds the depths below the knee to the same tolerance. Structures from the cryosection rules (ct_vhf_delt, ct_vhf_cuff, ct_vhf_armm, ct_vhf_pmr) carry the +-10 mm shoulder/arm registration uncertainty as well.",
  "Regenerated 2026-09-13 after the cryosection frame height correction (deltoid, rotator cuff, upper-arm muscles, pectoralis minor and the photograph part of the skin re-derived) and the male-to-female transfer (subject xfer_vhm2vhf: rows are estimates on her body, see docs/GEOMETRY_SOURCES.md 'Cross-subject transfer').",
  "Regenerated 2026-09-13, 20:20, after the deltoid rule v2 and the septa refinement (xfer_vhm2vhf_sep rows: transferred muscles with boundaries refined on her photographs)."
 ],
